From: lemonadep bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] pmap: form the physical address in pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys with ptoa()

pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys() passed `pp << PAGE_SHIFT' to flush_dcache()
as a physical address.  pp is a ppnum_t (uint32_t, osfmk/mach/vm_types.h:69)
and PAGE_SHIFT is an int, so the shift happens in 32 bits and the high half of
the physical address is dropped before the vm_offset_t cast.

On LEMONADEP all DRAM sits at or above 0x100000000 (phys 0x100000000,
5015 MiB), so every managed page has pp >= 0x40000 and the shift wraps to a
low address.  flush_dcache(..., phys=TRUE) hands that to phystokv_range(),
which panics in osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c:396:

	phystokv_range: illegal PA: 0x0; phys base 0x100000000, size ...

SWEET never saw this: its DRAM starts at 0x40000000, where the shift still
fits in 32 bits.  ptoa() (osfmk/mach/vm_param.h:113) casts to vm_address_t
before shifting, so it is identical for low physical addresses and correct
above 4 GiB.  The only caller is pmap_sync_wimg(), reached from
pmap_set_cache_attributes_priv() and pmap_update_compressor_page_internal()
when a page's WIMG attributes change.

diff --git a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
--- a/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm/pmap/pmap.c
@@ -6877,7 +6877,14 @@ void
 pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys(
 	ppnum_t pp)
 {
-	flush_dcache((vm_offset_t) (pp << PAGE_SHIFT), PAGE_SIZE, TRUE);
+	/*
+	 * ptoa() widens pp before the shift.  `pp << PAGE_SHIFT' is a 32-bit
+	 * shift (pp is a ppnum_t), so physical addresses at or above 4 GiB
+	 * wrap to a low address, and flush_dcache(phys=TRUE) then panics in
+	 * phystokv_range().  Boards whose DRAM starts at 4 GiB hit this on
+	 * every page.
+	 */
+	flush_dcache((vm_offset_t) ptoa(pp), PAGE_SIZE, TRUE);
 }
 
 #if CONFIG_COREDUMP
